                                    <h2><span class="shaft"><img id="184-0" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_o.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Omnidirectional" title="Omnidirectional" ><img id="184-1" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_c.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Cardioid" title="Cardioid" ><img id="184-2" src="//cdn.recordinghacks.com/images/icons/patterns/icon_8.png" width=27 height=27 alt="Bidirectional" title="Bidirectional" ></span>Blue Microphones Bottle</h2>
                    
                    <h2 class="sub">                    Detachable-Capsule Tube Condenser Microphone</h2>
                    <p>The Bottle is Blue&#8217;s flagship tube condenser, combining low noise and excellent transient response with a system of eight optional interchangeable capsules (called the &#8220;Bottle Caps&#8221;). </p><p>These bayonet-mount capsules can be exchanged to provide different tonal characteristics and pickup patterns while the power supply remains on. The Class A discrete amplifier circuit of The Bottle is a thoroughly modern homage to the past, with a design utilizing a single hand-selected EF86 pentode vacuum tube in triode mode. </p><p>To avoid the use of extraneous circuits which may degrade signal integrity, no pads or filters are incorporated into the Bottle&#8217;s schematic.</p><ul><li>Hand-built, hand-tuned, hand-tested</li><li>Class A discrete amplifier circuit with hand-selected EF86 pentode vacuum tube in triode mode</li><li>Capsules can be swapped &#8220;on the fly&#8221; for extreme versatility</li><li>Integrated capsule shockmounting</li><li>Custom wound output transformer</li><li>Includes B6 capsule, our renowned 9610 Tube Power Supply, Champagne tube mic cable, and ATA flight case</li></ul><p></p><blockquote><p><cite>Resolution Magazine</cite></p><p>By any measure, the Bottle is a stunning microphone &#8212; aesthetically, sonically and technically.</p></blockquote><p><p>Permalink: <a href="//recordinghacks.com/microphones/Blue-Microphones/Bottle">Blue Microphones Bottle</a></p><p>The mic was released in 1996.</p>
